<%# locals: () %>
<%# The way into the glossary (user, 04.11.2026): the glossary serves the
    transcription of meetings, so it is reached from the head of the meetings
    pages ("Alle Meetings" and a project's meetings), not from the sidebar.
    Only for those who may read it (GlossaryPolicy). A link of the whole page:
    the head stands beside frames, and the glossary is a page of its own.
    It leads to another page, so it is a word in cobalt (F5 of the
    Belegungstabelle), not a framed button: F2 is for an action. h-8 keeps it
    on the line of the head buttons beside it (F40). %>
<% if policy(GlossaryTerm).index? %>
  <%= link_to t('navigation.glossary'),
              organisation_glossary_terms_path(@current_organisation),
              class: 'inline-flex h-8 items-center rounded px-1 text-sm text-info no-underline ' \
                     'hover:underline focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-info',
              data: { turbo_frame: '_top', meetings_glossary_link: true } %>
<% end %>
